      <revisionDesc>
          <change when="2025-04-23T15:48:13-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready.</change>
          <change when="2025-01-13T05:42:17-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">Vote - AcceptText - first three good, though don't think ἀσπάζω needs to be reg'd (despite ἀσπάζομαι in l. 12), as it's a somewhat common late form, noted in LSJ and DGE, at least. In l. 17, there's certainly more than just one numeral, and ὡς would help with the sense. Maybe ξ̣ ὡ̣ς or else ξ̣ϛ</change>
          <change when="2024-12-31T11:47:30-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">Vote - AcceptText - The first three new readings look good. Not sure about the fourth (n.b. write stigma, not sigma)</change>
          <change when="2024-12-30T20:40:11-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Four corrections.</change>
          <change when="2024-12-30T20:39:36-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - In l. 14 accent on Ῥωμανὰν =&gt; Ῥωμάναν.</change>
          <change when="2024-12-30T20:36:47-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Commit - In lin9 ἀσπάζομ =&gt; ἀσπάζω (l. ἀσπάζομαι), cf. the omega in εὐχῶν. In lin11-12 there is a male slave called Achilles: τὴν δούλην =&gt; τὸ̣[ν] δο̣ῦ̣λον; Ἀχειλλί̣δαν =&gt; Ἀχειλλέαν (ex corr. Ἀχειλλεον, l. Ἀχιλλέα). In lin17 there should be a number of the knidia mentioned, and ὡς is difficult. I read ὡς =&gt; ς̣ (six).</change>
